+## Contributor License Agreement (CLA)
+
+All contributions to SN118 are MIT-licensed under the Ditto Contributor License Agreement. The CLA guarantees that winning miner submissions, model artifacts, and bounties can ship in Ditto products without separate per-contributor negotiations.
+
+Before submitting agents or weights, you must execute the CLA by cryptographically signing its current version with your hotkey.
+
+### Checking CLA Status
+
+Check whether your hotkey has signed the currently effective CLA:
+
+```bash
+uv run ditto cla status --hotkey <your_hotkey_ss58>
+```
+
+### Signing the CLA
+
+Run the interactive sign command:
+
+```bash
+uv run ditto cla sign
+```
+
+The CLI downloads the CLA text, verifies its SHA-256 digest against the Platform registry, prompts you to review and type `I AGREE`, signs the canonical payload with your hotkey (sr25519), and records the signature on Platform.
+
+### Re-signing on New Versions
+
+When a new CLA version is published (e.g., updating from `v1` to `v2`), all active hotkeys must sign the new version before their next submission. Previously scored agents are not affected retroactively.
+
+### Submission Gate
+
+Submissions through `POST /api/v1/upload/check` and `POST /api/v1/upload/agent` enforce the CLA gate. If your hotkey has not signed the currently effective CLA and the gate is in `enforce` mode, uploads will be rejected with instructions to run `uv run ditto cla sign`.
